file tools/fixtures/caravan_ladder_print_scan.sh the third meter -- three readings over the printing family, a named ceiling, TAME's ratchet reported, three refusals by name
file tools/caravan_ladder_print_witness.rish pulls the scan every lap beside its two kin, asserts each reading, proves the counter on a hand-countable corpus, and refuses three RED paths on metal
file tools/fixtures/caravan_ladder_print_corpus/foot.rye the corpus foot -- one three-line telling
file tools/fixtures/caravan_ladder_print_corpus/top.rye the rung above -- the foot's telling byte for byte, beside a staircase of it, so the corpus holds both shapes the scan reads
file crux/REMEMBER.md live edge refreshed to the printing meter; the prior edge folded down one line
recommend keep-going the printing carry is a number now, and its split names the fold's two halves. Lift the 93 byte-identical bodies into `caravan/ladder_checks.rye` first -- that is fold B's move, already done twice on this ladder, and it takes 3,164 lines with it. Then take the staircase the way fold D took the spine, one body over the `comptime` seam the harness already holds. Both halves have their seam written; what was missing was the number, and the number now stands under a ceiling that will catch the next rung before the fold does.
